cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or methodology, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "QACLDN: Quantum Actor-Critic for Drone Navigation — A Hybrid Quantum-Classical Reinforcement Learning Pipeline with Empirical Real-Data Calibration"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "<this-repository-url>"
abstract: >
  A from-scratch, dependency-free implementation and empirical evaluation of
  QACLDN (Quantum Actor-Critic for Drone Navigation): a hybrid
  quantum-classical policy-gradient method for UAV obstacle-avoidance
  navigation. Includes a batched NumPy statevector VQC simulator with an
  exact parameter-shift gradient rule (verified to 1e-11 against finite
  differences), a 12-state RK4-integrated rigid-body quadrotor dynamics
  engine, and empirical calibration against three real-world data sources
  (UAV telemetry, ICMCIS multi-sensor drone-detection radar/RF logs, and the
  gym-pybullet-drones cf2x physical parameter specification).
keywords:
  - quantum machine learning
  - variational quantum circuits
  - reinforcement learning
  - quantum reinforcement learning
  - UAV navigation
  - drone obstacle avoidance
  - actor-critic
  - parameter-shift rule
  - hybrid quantum-classical algorithms
